Here’s the exact request you’d send to VirusTotal to pull the **sub‑domain** relationships for `example.org`, limited to 10 results and starting at the cursor `abc`.  
Only the related object IDs (and any context attributes) will be returned – no other fields.

```http
GET https://www.virustotal.com/api/v3/domains/example.org/relationships/subdomains?limit=10&continuation_cursor=abc
Host: www.virustotal.com
Accept: application/json
x-apikey: my_api
```

**What you’ll receive**

```json
{
  "data": [
    {
      "id": "sub1.example.org",
      "type": "domain",
      "attributes": {
        "context_attributes": { ... }   // optional context data
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "sub2.example.org",
      "type": "domain",
      "attributes": {
        "context_attributes": { ... }
      }
    },
    ...
  ],
  "meta": {
    "continuation_cursor": "next_cursor_value_if_more_results"
  }
}
```

Feel free to copy the request into your preferred HTTP client (curl, Postman, etc.) and replace `my_api` with your actual API key.
